Notebook[{Cell["Paper-Matched Radial Coordinate and Areal-Gauge Certificate", 
   "Title"], 
  Cell[
   "Generic unequal charges, static exact map, and exact-in-j pullback rule", 
   "Subtitle"], Cell["Purpose and scope", "Section"], 
  Cell[TextData[{"This notebook independently certifies the first-order \
radial diffeomorphism between the paper/isotropic-like static coordinate and \
the areal (Schwarzschild-like) gauge used to solve the reduced equations.  It \
is self-contained: all twelve unequal-charge areal-gauge correction functions \
and all paper-coordinate formulas are literal data in this notebook.  No \
project file is loaded when it is evaluated."}], "Text"], 
  Cell[TextData[{"The coupling convention is ", 
     StyleBox["lambda3 = alphaPrime/8", FontFamily -> "Courier"], ".  Every \
correction function below is the coefficient of lambda3, so its coefficient \
of alphaPrime is one eighth as large.  The proof is exact at first order in \
that coupling and does not expand in the three charges."}], "Text"], 
  Cell[TextData[{"Source locations used for transcription: arXiv:2502.05065, \
the field-redefined static solution and its spherical-coordinate form in BH \
Final V2.tex lines 841--913 (SHA-256 dd1d3314...9789); arXiv:2603.18180, the \
repeated and generic-lambda_I solution in Superinvariant-final.tex lines \
1012--1061 (SHA-256 2ddd7566...d226); v3 notebook 13, Section 5, lines \
203257--203304 (SHA-256 208760ff...0403); and static_lambda3_seed_areal.wl \
(SHA-256 938395c7...88aa)."}], "Text"], Cell["Important terminology", 
   "Subsection"], Cell[TextData[{"The paper coordinate is called \
isotropic-like, not strictly isotropic.  After the field redefinitions used \
in the five-dimensional Riemann frame, the published spatial metric contains \
a distinguished radial tensor correction (called deltaG3RadialPaper below), \
so it is not exactly conformally flat.  The areal gauge instead fixes the \
first-order correction to the angular sphere-size exponent to zero."}], 
   "Text"], Cell["1. Exact arithmetic and branch", "Section"], 
  Cell[BoxData["ClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\n$HistoryLength=0; \
$RecursionLimit=200000;\nphysicalBranch=R>0&&q1+R^2>0&&q2+R^2>0&&q3+R^2>0;\ne\
xactZeroQ[expression_]:=TrueQ[Expand[Numerator[Together[expression]]]===0];\n\
derivativeAt[function_,argument_]:=Module[{dummy},D[function[dummy],dummy]/.d\
ummy->argument];"], "Input"], Cell["2. Paper/isotropic-like static fields", 
   "Section"], Cell[TextData[{"The variable r in this section is the paper \
radius.  The functions dLogHI are radial derivatives of log(HI).  The symbols \
deltaFPaper, deltaGPaper and deltaHPaper are corrections to metric exponents, \
with deltaHPaper controlling the angular sphere size.  The gauge-field \
convention is the positive STU convention A^1=A, A^2=-B, A^3=C, so all \
leading electric potentials are +1/HI.  The scalar functions are the \
canonical report variables varphi1 and varphi2.  Only at the literal \
seed-comparison boundary are they converted to the old notebook coordinates \
P=-Sqrt[6] deltaVarphi1/4 and S=deltaVarphi2/Sqrt[2]."}], "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData["H1Paper[r_]:=1+q1/r^2; H2Paper[r_]:=1+q2/r^2; \
H3Paper[r_]:=1+q3/r^2;\nHProductPaper[r_]:=H1Paper[r] H2Paper[r] \
H3Paper[r];\ndLogH1[r_]:=-2 q1/(r (q1+r^2)); dLogH2[r_]:=-2 q2/(r (q2+r^2)); \
dLogH3[r_]:=-2 q3/(r \
(q3+r^2));\ndLogHProduct[r_]:=dLogH1[r]+dLogH2[r]+dLogH3[r];\ndeltaU1Paper[r_\
]:=2 dLogHProduct[r] (dLogH1[r]+dLogH2[r])/(3 H1Paper[r] \
H3Paper[r]);\ndeltaU2Paper[r_]:=2 dLogHProduct[r] (dLogH1[r]+dLogH2[r])/(3 \
H2Paper[r] H3Paper[r]);\ndeltaU3Paper[r_]:=-2 dLogHProduct[r] dLogH3[r]/(3 \
H3Paper[r]^2);\ndeltaVarphi1Paper[r_]:=-4 dLogHProduct[r]^2/(Sqrt[6] 6 \
H3Paper[r]); deltaVarphi2Paper[r_]:=0;\ndeltaG1Paper[r_]:=2/(9 H3Paper[r]) (7 \
(dLogH1[r]-dLogH2[r])^2-2 (dLogH1[r]+dLogH2[r]) dLogH3[r]+19 \
dLogH3[r]^2);\ndeltaG2Paper[r_]:=4/(9 H3Paper[r]) \
((dLogH1[r]-dLogH2[r])^2+(dLogH1[r]+dLogH2[r]) dLogH3[r]+4 \
dLogH3[r]^2);\ndeltaG3RadialPaper[r_]:=4/(9 H3Paper[r]) (dLogHProduct[r]^2+3 \
dLogHProduct[r] \
dLogH3[r]);\ndeltaFPaper[r_]:=-deltaG1Paper[r]/2;\ndeltaGPaper[r_]:=(deltaG2P\
aper[r]-deltaG3RadialPaper[r])/2;\ndeltaHPaper[r_]:=deltaG2Paper[r]/2;\nF0[r_\
]:=-Log[HProductPaper[r]]/3; G0[r_]:=Log[HProductPaper[r]]/6; \
H0[r_]:=Log[HProductPaper[r]]/6;\nVarphi10[r_]:=Log[H1Paper[r] \
H2Paper[r]/H3Paper[r]^2]/Sqrt[6];\nVarphi20[r_]:=Log[H1Paper[r]/H2Paper[r]]/S\
qrt[2];\nU10[r_]:=1/H1Paper[r]; U20[r_]:=1/H2Paper[r]; \
U30[r_]:=1/H3Paper[r];\npaperLambda3Coefficients={deltaU1Paper[R],deltaU2Pape\
r[R],deltaU3Paper[R],deltaVarphi1Paper[R],deltaVarphi2Paper[R],deltaFPaper[R]\
,deltaGPaper[R],deltaHPaper[R]};\ncouplingNormalizationChecks=And@@(TrueQ[Exp\
and[((lambda3 #)/.lambda3->alphaPrime/8)-alphaPrime \
(#/8)]===0]&/@paperLambda3Coefficients);\npaperTemporalBracket=7 \
(dLogH1[R]-dLogH2[R])^2-2 (dLogH1[R]+dLogH2[R]) dLogH3[R]+19 \
dLogH3[R]^2;\npaperAngularBracket=(dLogH1[R]-dLogH2[R])^2+(dLogH1[R]+dLogH2[R\
]) dLogH3[R]+4 dLogH3[R]^2;\npaperRadialMultiplier=-2 (dLogH1[R] \
dLogH2[R]+(dLogH1[R]+dLogH2[R]) dLogH3[R])/(9 \
H3Paper[R]);\npaperTranscriptionChecks=<|\"A^1 electric \
coefficient\"->exactZeroQ[deltaU1Paper[R]/8-dLogHProduct[R] \
(dLogH1[R]+dLogH2[R])/(12 H1Paper[R] H3Paper[R])],\"A^2=-B electric \
coefficient\"->exactZeroQ[deltaU2Paper[R]/8-dLogHProduct[R] \
(dLogH1[R]+dLogH2[R])/(12 H2Paper[R] H3Paper[R])],\"A^3 electric \
coefficient\"->exactZeroQ[deltaU3Paper[R]/8+dLogHProduct[R] dLogH3[R]/(12 \
H3Paper[R]^2)],\"heterotic dilaton coefficient\"->exactZeroQ[(-Sqrt[6] \
deltaVarphi1Paper[R]/4)/8-dLogHProduct[R]^2/(48 H3Paper[R])],\"temporal \
metric multiplier\"->exactZeroQ[deltaFPaper[R]/4+paperTemporalBracket/(36 \
H3Paper[R])],\"radial metric \
multiplier\"->exactZeroQ[deltaGPaper[R]/4-paperRadialMultiplier],\"angular \
metric multiplier\"->exactZeroQ[deltaHPaper[R]/4-paperAngularBracket/(18 \
H3Paper[R])]|>;\n<|\"lambda3=alphaPrime/8\"->couplingNormalizationChecks,\"Pu\
blishedAlphaPrimeCoefficients\"->paperTranscriptionChecks|>"], "Input"], 
  Cell["3. The radial map to areal gauge", "Section"], 
  Cell[TextData[{"Let the paper radius and areal radius be related by rPaper \
= R + lambda3 xiStatic(R).  A scalar-like correction gains +xiStatic times \
the background radial derivative.  The radial metric exponent also gains \
xiStatic prime from the Jacobian.  The angular exponent gains xiStatic (H0 \
prime + 1/R), including the explicit radius multiplying the unit \
three-sphere."}], "Text"], Cell[BoxData["xiStatic[R_]:=Together[-deltaHPaper[\
R]/(derivativeAt[H0,R]+1/R)];\nscalarPaperToAreal[paperCorrection_,background\
_][R_]:=Together[paperCorrection[R]+xiStatic[R] \
derivativeAt[background,R]];\nradialExponentPaperToAreal[R_]:=Together[deltaG\
Paper[R]+xiStatic[R] \
derivativeAt[G0,R]+derivativeAt[xiStatic,R]];\nsphereExponentPaperToAreal[R_]\
:=Together[deltaHPaper[R]+xiStatic[R] \
(derivativeAt[H0,R]+1/R)];\ncandidateArealCorrections={scalarPaperToAreal[del\
taU1Paper,U10][R],scalarPaperToAreal[deltaU2Paper,U20][R],scalarPaperToAreal[\
deltaU3Paper,U30][R],0,0,0,-Sqrt[6] \
scalarPaperToAreal[deltaVarphi1Paper,Varphi10][R]/4,scalarPaperToAreal[deltaV\
arphi2Paper,Varphi20][R]/Sqrt[2],scalarPaperToAreal[deltaFPaper,F0][R],radial\
ExponentPaperToAreal[R],0,0};\ngaugeDenominator=q1 q2+q1 q3+q2 q3+2 R^2 \
(q1+q2+q3)+3 \
R^4;\npositiveDenominator=(q1+R^2)(q2+R^2)+(q1+R^2)(q3+R^2)+(q2+R^2)(q3+R^2);\
\ncoordinateGaugeChecks=<|\"SphereCorrectionVanishes\"->exactZeroQ[sphereExpo\
nentPaperToAreal[R]],\"PositiveDenominatorIdentity\"->exactZeroQ[gaugeDenomin\
ator-positiveDenominator],\"ShiftIsJIndependent\"->FreeQ[xiStatic[R],jrot]|>;\
\n<|\"rPaperEquals\"->HoldForm[R+lambda3 \
xiStatic[R]],\"XiStatic\"->Factor[xiStatic[R]],\"Checks\"->coordinateGaugeChe\
cks|>"], "Input"], Cell["4. Embedded v3 areal representative", "Section"], 
  Cell[TextData[{"The next cell is literal data copied from the independently \
derived generic static seed.  It is intentionally verbose: this makes the \
comparison executable without any cache, import statement, or path \
dependency."}], "Text"], Cell[BoxData["staticArealSeedRules={U1 -> \
Function[{z}, (8*(-12*q1^3*q2^3*q3^2 + 2*q1^3*q2^3*q3*z - \n      \
28*q1^3*q2^2*q3^2*z - 16*q1^2*q2^3*q3^2*z + 4*q1^3*q2^3*z^2 + \n      \
13*q1^3*q2^2*q3*z^2 + 17*q1^2*q2^3*q3*z^2 - 27*q1^3*q2*q3^2*z^2 - \n      \
32*q1^2*q2^2*q3^2*z^2 - 5*q1*q2^3*q3^2*z^2 + 12*q1^3*q2^2*z^3 + \n      \
12*q1^2*q2^3*z^3 + 8*q1^3*q2*q3*z^3 + 62*q1^2*q2^2*q3*z^3 + \n      \
14*q1*q2^3*q3*z^3 - 10*q1^3*q3^2*z^3 - 32*q1^2*q2*q3^2*z^3 - \n      \
8*q1*q2^2*q3^2*z^3 + 2*q2^3*q3^2*z^3 + 7*q1^3*q2*z^4 + \n      \
34*q1^2*q2^2*z^4 + 7*q1*q2^3*z^4 - q1^3*q3*z^4 + 47*q1^2*q2*q3*z^4 + \n      \
41*q1*q2^2*q3*z^4 + 5*q2^3*q3*z^4 - 13*q1^2*q3^2*z^4 - \n      \
12*q1*q2*q3^2*z^4 + 5*q2^2*q3^2*z^4 + 22*q1^2*q2*z^5 + 16*q1*q2^2*z^5 + \n    \
  2*q2^3*z^5 + 8*q1^2*q3*z^5 + 24*q1*q2*q3*z^5 + 10*q2^2*q3*z^5 - \n      \
6*q1*q3^2*z^5 + 2*q2*q3^2*z^5 + 3*q1^2*z^6 + 6*q1*q2*z^6 + 3*q2^2*z^6 + \n    \
  3*q1*q3*z^6 + 3*q2*q3*z^6))/(3*(q1 + z)^3*(q2 + z)^2*(q3 + z)^2*\n     \
(q1*q2 + q1*q3 + q2*q3 + 2*q1*z + 2*q2*z + 2*q3*z + 3*z^2))], \n U2 -> \
Function[{z}, (8*(-12*q1^3*q2^3*q3^2 + 2*q1^3*q2^3*q3*z - \n      \
16*q1^3*q2^2*q3^2*z - 28*q1^2*q2^3*q3^2*z + 4*q1^3*q2^3*z^2 + \n      \
17*q1^3*q2^2*q3*z^2 + 13*q1^2*q2^3*q3*z^2 - 5*q1^3*q2*q3^2*z^2 - \n      \
32*q1^2*q2^2*q3^2*z^2 - 27*q1*q2^3*q3^2*z^2 + 12*q1^3*q2^2*z^3 + \n      \
12*q1^2*q2^3*z^3 + 14*q1^3*q2*q3*z^3 + 62*q1^2*q2^2*q3*z^3 + \n      \
8*q1*q2^3*q3*z^3 + 2*q1^3*q3^2*z^3 - 8*q1^2*q2*q3^2*z^3 - \n      \
32*q1*q2^2*q3^2*z^3 - 10*q2^3*q3^2*z^3 + 7*q1^3*q2*z^4 + \n      \
34*q1^2*q2^2*z^4 + 7*q1*q2^3*z^4 + 5*q1^3*q3*z^4 + 41*q1^2*q2*q3*z^4 + \n     \
 47*q1*q2^2*q3*z^4 - q2^3*q3*z^4 + 5*q1^2*q3^2*z^4 - 12*q1*q2*q3^2*z^4 - \n   \
   13*q2^2*q3^2*z^4 + 2*q1^3*z^5 + 16*q1^2*q2*z^5 + 22*q1*q2^2*z^5 + \n      \
10*q1^2*q3*z^5 + 24*q1*q2*q3*z^5 + 8*q2^2*q3*z^5 + 2*q1*q3^2*z^5 - \n      \
6*q2*q3^2*z^5 + 3*q1^2*z^6 + 6*q1*q2*z^6 + 3*q2^2*z^6 + 3*q1*q3*z^6 + \n      \
3*q2*q3*z^6))/(3*(q1 + z)^2*(q2 + z)^3*(q3 + z)^2*\n     (q1*q2 + q1*q3 + \
q2*q3 + 2*q1*z + 2*q2*z + 2*q3*z + 3*z^2))], \n U3 -> Function[{z}, \
(-8*q3*(12*q1^2*q2^2*q3^2 + 7*q1^2*q2^2*q3*z + \n      25*q1^2*q2*q3^2*z + \
25*q1*q2^2*q3^2*z + 2*q1^2*q2^2*z^2 + \n      16*q1^2*q2*q3*z^2 + \
16*q1*q2^2*q3*z^2 + 14*q1^2*q3^2*z^2 + \n      46*q1*q2*q3^2*z^2 + \
14*q2^2*q3^2*z^2 + 5*q1^2*q2*z^3 + 5*q1*q2^2*z^3 + \n      11*q1^2*q3*z^3 + \
24*q1*q2*q3*z^3 + 11*q2^2*q3*z^3 + 23*q1*q3^2*z^3 + \n      23*q2*q3^2*z^3 + \
4*q1^2*z^4 + 6*q1*q2*z^4 + 4*q2^2*z^4 + 12*q1*q3*z^4 + \n      12*q2*q3*z^4 + \
10*q3^2*z^4 + 3*q1*z^5 + 3*q2*z^5 + 3*q3*z^5))/\n    (3*(q1 + z)*(q2 + z)*(q3 \
+ z)^4*(q1*q2 + q1*q3 + q2*q3 + 2*q1*z + \n      2*q2*z + 2*q3*z + 3*z^2))], \
B1 -> Function[{z}, 0], \n B2 -> Function[{z}, 0], B3 -> Function[{z}, 0], \n \
P -> Function[{z}, (2*(-15*q1^3*q2^3*q3^2 + 21*q1^3*q2^2*q3^3 + \n      \
21*q1^2*q2^3*q3^3 + 4*q1^3*q2^3*q3*z - 10*q1^3*q2^2*q3^2*z - \n      \
10*q1^2*q2^3*q3^2*z + 34*q1^3*q2*q3^3*z + 110*q1^2*q2^2*q3^3*z + \n      \
34*q1*q2^3*q3^3*z + 4*q1^3*q2^3*z^2 + 26*q1^3*q2^2*q3*z^2 + \n      \
26*q1^2*q2^3*q3*z^2 + 2*q1^3*q2*q3^2*z^2 + 45*q1^2*q2^2*q3^2*z^2 + \n      \
2*q1*q2^3*q3^2*z^2 + 16*q1^3*q3^3*z^2 + 134*q1^2*q2*q3^3*z^2 + \n      \
134*q1*q2^2*q3^3*z^2 + 16*q2^3*q3^3*z^2 + 12*q1^3*q2^2*z^3 + \n      \
12*q1^2*q2^3*z^3 + 18*q1^3*q2*q3*z^3 + 108*q1^2*q2^2*q3*z^3 + \n      \
18*q1*q2^3*q3*z^3 + 6*q1^3*q3^2*z^3 + 54*q1^2*q2*q3^2*z^3 + \n      \
54*q1*q2^2*q3^2*z^3 + 6*q2^3*q3^2*z^3 + 54*q1^2*q3^3*z^3 + \n      \
144*q1*q2*q3^3*z^3 + 54*q2^2*q3^3*z^3 + 5*q1^3*q2*z^4 + \n      \
38*q1^2*q2^2*z^4 + 5*q1*q2^3*z^4 + 5*q1^3*q3*z^4 + 75*q1^2*q2*q3*z^4 + \n     \
 75*q1*q2^2*q3*z^4 + 5*q2^3*q3*z^4 + 26*q1^2*q3^2*z^4 + \n      \
39*q1*q2*q3^2*z^4 + 26*q2^2*q3^2*z^4 + 53*q1*q3^3*z^4 + \n      \
53*q2*q3^3*z^4 + 20*q1^2*q2*z^5 + 20*q1*q2^2*z^5 + 20*q1^2*q3*z^5 + \n      \
36*q1*q2*q3*z^5 + 20*q2^2*q3*z^5 + 14*q1*q3^2*z^5 + 14*q2*q3^2*z^5 + \n      \
18*q3^3*z^5 + 3*q1^2*z^6 + 6*q1*q2*z^6 + 3*q2^2*z^6 + 6*q1*q3*z^6 + \n      \
6*q2*q3*z^6 + 3*q3^2*z^6))/(3*(q1 + z)^2*(q2 + z)^2*(q3 + z)^3*\n     (q1*q2 \
+ q1*q3 + q2*q3 + 2*q1*z + 2*q2*z + 2*q3*z + 3*z^2))], \n S -> Function[{z}, \
(8*(q1 - q2)*(6*q1^2*q2^2*q3^2 + 2*q1^2*q2^2*q3*z + \n      11*q1^2*q2*q3^2*z \
+ 11*q1*q2^2*q3^2*z + 3*q1^2*q2*q3*z^2 + \n      3*q1*q2^2*q3*z^2 + \
6*q1^2*q3^2*z^2 + 18*q1*q2*q3^2*z^2 + \n      6*q2^2*q3^2*z^2 + 3*q1^2*q3*z^3 \
+ 3*q2^2*q3*z^3 + 9*q1*q3^2*z^3 + \n      9*q2*q3^2*z^3 + q1^2*z^4 - \
2*q1*q2*z^4 + q2^2*z^4 + q1*q3*z^4 + \n      q2*q3*z^4 + 4*q3^2*z^4))/(3*(q1 \
+ z)^2*(q2 + z)^2*(q3 + z)^2*\n     (q1*q2 + q1*q3 + q2*q3 + 2*q1*z + 2*q2*z \
+ 2*q3*z + 3*z^2))], \n Ft -> Function[{z}, (-4*(24*q1^3*q2^3*q3^3 + \
29*q1^3*q2^3*q3^2*z + \n      65*q1^3*q2^2*q3^3*z + 65*q1^2*q2^3*q3^3*z + \
4*q1^3*q2^3*q3*z^2 + \n      74*q1^3*q2^2*q3^2*z^2 + 74*q1^2*q2^3*q3^2*z^2 + \
64*q1^3*q2*q3^3*z^2 + \n      170*q1^2*q2^2*q3^3*z^2 + 64*q1*q2^3*q3^3*z^2 + \
6*q1^3*q2^2*q3*z^3 + \n      6*q1^2*q2^3*q3*z^3 + 78*q1^3*q2*q3^2*z^3 + \
165*q1^2*q2^2*q3^2*z^3 + \n      78*q1*q2^3*q3^2*z^3 + 24*q1^3*q3^3*z^3 + \
162*q1^2*q2*q3^3*z^3 + \n      162*q1*q2^2*q3^3*z^3 + 24*q2^3*q3^3*z^3 + \
16*q1^3*q2*q3*z^4 - \n      24*q1^2*q2^2*q3*z^4 + 16*q1*q2^3*q3*z^4 + \
36*q1^3*q3^2*z^4 + \n      156*q1^2*q2*q3^2*z^4 + 156*q1*q2^2*q3^2*z^4 + \
36*q2^3*q3^2*z^4 + \n      60*q1^2*q3^3*z^4 + 148*q1*q2*q3^3*z^4 + \
60*q2^2*q3^3*z^4 + \n      5*q1^3*q2*z^5 - 10*q1^2*q2^2*z^5 + 5*q1*q2^3*z^5 + \
17*q1^3*q3*z^5 - \n      21*q1^2*q2*q3*z^5 - 21*q1*q2^2*q3*z^5 + \
17*q2^3*q3*z^5 + \n      74*q1^2*q3^2*z^5 + 123*q1*q2*q3^2*z^5 + \
74*q2^2*q3^2*z^5 + \n      53*q1*q3^3*z^5 + 53*q2*q3^3*z^5 + 6*q1^3*z^6 - \
6*q1^2*q2*z^6 - \n      6*q1*q2^2*z^6 + 6*q2^3*z^6 + 18*q1^2*q3*z^6 - \
48*q1*q2*q3*z^6 + \n      18*q2^2*q3*z^6 + 54*q1*q3^2*z^6 + 54*q2*q3^2*z^6 + \
18*q3^3*z^6 + \n      7*q1^2*z^7 - 14*q1*q2*z^7 + 7*q2^2*z^7 - 2*q1*q3*z^7 - \
2*q2*q3*z^7 + \n      19*q3^2*z^7))/(3*z*(q1 + z)^2*(q2 + z)^2*(q3 + z)^3*\n  \
   (q1*q2 + q1*q3 + q2*q3 + 2*q1*z + 2*q2*z + 2*q3*z + 3*z^2))], \n Gr -> \
Function[{z}, (8*(36*q1^4*q2^4*q3^3 + 36*q1^4*q2^3*q3^4 + \n      \
